npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# MCP config — contains a Supabase access token (secret); never commit
.mcp.json

# Claude Code local tooling, plans & machine-specific settings.
#
# THE FOUR raagam-* SKILLS SHIP WITH THE REPO; everything else here stays local.
#
# They are not optional reading. `doc/ui/LAYOUT.md` §8 tells a developer that the
# keyboard contract "lives in .claude/skills/raagam-keyboard-contract", and
# `doc/ui/uicheck list.md` calls it "the authoritative version" — while `.claude/`
# was ignored wholesale, so a fresh clone contained neither. Both documents have
# been pointing at something nobody but the author could read.
#
# ORDER MATTERS AND IS NOT OBVIOUS. Git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so `!.claude/skills/...` under a plain `.claude/` rule can never
# match — the walk stops at `.claude` and the re-include is dead text. Each level
# is therefore excluded by its CONTENTS (`dir/*`) and the next level re-included
# by name, all the way down. Once a directory is re-included its files come with
# it, which is why there is no fifth line.
#
# Verify with the catalog, not by reading:
#   git check-ignore -v .claude/skills/raagam-screen-layout/SKILL.md   → no output
#   git check-ignore -v .claude/skills/docx/SKILL.md                   → a match
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/raagam-*/

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Local dev-server log capture
.devlog.txt

# Vocabulary miner (scripts/mine-name-vocabularies.mts) — both regenerated on
# demand. The 668 KB HSN workbook is a cached download, and the proposal file is
# a working document: what gets KEPT from it lands in name-vocabularies.ts, which
# is committed. Committing the proposals instead would turn a reviewed decision
# back into a list of maybes.
/scripts/.vocab-cache/
/scripts/out/

# Python bytecode from scripts/audit_layout.py — regenerated on every run
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# MSYS/Git-Bash crash dumps, written into the repo root where the shell was
*.stackdump
